  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility study and pilot for digital currency and banking system for the unbanked</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since its establishment in 2015, Blockbonds&apos; focus has been to develop technology solutions for the financial industry. Blockbonds is the first company to digitise a national currency by correlating the digital funds on the platform 1-to-1 with the local currency in the market. The main objectives of this project is to evaluate a full operational launch and establish a foothold in Tanzania together with the bank partner I&amp;M Bank, and to evaluate the feasibility of establishing SPENN in four new markets: Kenya, Uganda, Ghana and Ethiopia. The feasibility study will include an in-depth analysis to assess the market attractiveness and SPENN&#x2019;s position to compete, as well as a due diligence on prospective bank partners and overall fit with existing markets.</narrative>
  </description>
